    {
      "id": "73c71835-307a-4079-a4a6-cdcc439a5c3c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -336,
        -1040
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1080,
        "content": "## Grid Frequency Anomaly Monitor\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow polls grid frequency telemetry for a region, computes each substation's deviation from nominal frequency and its rate-of-change-of-frequency (ROCOF), and classifies stability into Normal / Watch / Warning / Critical. Anomalous regions are enriched with recent historical stability context, turned into an operator-facing alert, and pushed to the grid operator dashboard. Critical-tier events additionally open a formal grid stability incident.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the grid telemetry API URL, region, and credentials in \"Fetch Grid Frequency Readings\".\n- Set nominalFrequencyHz and the watch/warning/critical deviation + ROCOF thresholds in the config node to match your grid's standard (e.g. 50Hz or 60Hz).\n- Configure the historical-events API, operator dashboard API, and incident-system API URLs and credentials in their respective HTTP Request nodes.\n- Verify the telemetry response shape matches what the code nodes expect: { regions: [ { regionId, regionName, readings: [ { timestamp, frequencyHz }, ... ] } ] }.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the deviation/ROCOF thresholds, polling interval, historical lookback window, and incident payload fields to match your grid operator's runbook."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "480a7280-c124-40ce-86bf-3ea77ff27ce7",
